Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 03:07:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [Model] Add SKT A.X K2 (axk2)

A.X K2 is a 688B-total / 33B-active Mixture-of-Experts decoder-only model
(256 routed + 1 shared expert, 8 routed experts per token, 61 layers) released
by SKT under Apache-2.0. The published checkpoint is block-scaled FP8 (E4M3).

Architecturally it builds on the DeepSeek-V3 MLA layout and adds:

- Sparse Gated Attention (SGA): a lightweight indexer scores key-value
  candidates and selects top-k (k=2048) per query, combined with a
  head-specific output gate on the attention output. The gate is fused into
  q_b_proj at load time.
- Gated Norm: an input-dependent low-rank gate applied after RMSNorm, which
  suppresses massive activations and keeps the activation distribution
  friendly to narrow low-precision formats.

Adds the model implementation and config class, and registers model_type
"axk2" so MLA is selected for it. MLA head_size is kv_lora_rank +
qk_rope_head_dim = 512 + 64 = 576, which the FlashMLA kernels accept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
